
We are using the Plan9 Ansi Posix Environment (APE), pdcurses [1], pcre [2] and lua [3].
The port assumes that you have built and installed pdcurses and lua and that your header files have the #pragma lib .
For regex, the port is using pcre, which also has been ported to plan9.

Current attempts are using a patched/forked/expanded version of APE to deal with various compiler capabilities [4]. This patched APE also includes all the build dependencies.

The plan9 port is using a lot from "unix", but we do not have tty so we depend on curses.

To build, just run mk in his directory or run ./build.rc to also build the nethack helper programs.
 
TODO in the future: A native /dev/draw windowing system for NetHack to have a more native-looking client with more advanced graphics capabilities.


Dependencies with Plan9 (9front) APE ports:

[1] https://github.com/Bill-Gray/PDCursesMod (upstream)
[2] https://github.com/staalmannen/pcre (fork)
[3] https://github.com/staalmannen/Lua (fork)
[4] https://github.com/staalmannen/APExp
